    "qualifierLines": [
      "{**30 NY3d at 739} OPINION OF THE COURT",
      "Defense counsel challenged the 25 points, arguing that because a YO adjudication is not a conviction, it may not be considered as part of defendant's criminal history for the purposes of SORA. The SORA court rejected this objection and designated defendant a level three sexually violent sex offender. The Appellate Division affirmed the level three designation, with one Justice dissenting (, 137 AD3d 91 [2d Dept 2016]). We granted leave to appeal (People v Francis, 27 NY3d 908 [2016])."
    ],
